{title: Alas! and Did My Saviour Bleed}
{artist: Isaac Watts / Ralph E. Hudson}
{genre: Easter}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 143장}
{title_ko: 웬말인가 날 위하여}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[G]las! and did my [C]Saviour [G]bleed
And [G]did my [D]Sovereign [G]die
Would [G]He devote that [C]sacred [G]head
For [G]such a [D]worm as [G]I
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
At the [G]cross, at the cross, where I [C]first saw the [G]light
And the [G]burden of my [D]heart rolled a[G]way
It was [G]there by faith I [C]received my [G]sight
And [G]now I am [D]happy all the [G]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Was [G]it for crimes that [C]I have [G]done
He [G]groaned up[D]on the [G]tree
A[G]mazing pity, [C]grace un[G]known
And [G]love be[D]yond de[G]gree
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Well [G]might the sun in [C]darkness [G]hide
And [G]shut his [D]glories [G]in
When [G]Christ, the mighty [C]Maker [G]died
For [G]man the [D]creature's [G]sin
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
But [G]drops of grief can [C]ne'er re[G]pay
The [G]debt of [D]love I [G]owe
Here, [G]Lord, I give my[C]self a[G]way
'Tis [G]all that [D]I can [G]do
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
